WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:06.220
The CW's Riverdale promised a sexy, updated
take on the classic Archie comics series,

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.320
and thus far, the show has delivered.

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:12.410
Taking the comics' central group of teens
and placing them smack dab in the middle of

00:00:12.410 --> 00:00:17.720
a burgeoning murder mystery, Riverdale has
the intrigue, sass, and fun of a bona fide

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:18.720
hit.

00:00:18.720 --> 00:00:22.590
It also has taken a lot of liberties with
how the characters appear and act compared

00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:23.590
to the comics.

00:00:23.590 --> 00:00:27.279
Here's a peek at how the cast of Riverdale
should really look.

00:00:27.279 --> 00:00:28.710
Archie Andrews

00:00:28.710 --> 00:00:32.980
Archie is one of the most famous redheads
in pop culture, so of course actor K.J.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:36.550
Apa would have to dye his naturally brown
hair red for the part.

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:41.630
However, despite the fact that Apa spent ten
hours in a salon struggling to get the "right

00:00:41.630 --> 00:00:45.620
shade of orange," it's nowhere near as light
as Archie's hair from the comics.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:48.770
Apa is also missing the character's signature
freckles.

00:00:48.770 --> 00:00:51.230
They did get the eyebrows pretty much perfect,
though.

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.910
Of course, the show also had to CW-ify Archie
a little.

00:00:54.910 --> 00:00:55.910
"Oh..

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:57.150
My God!"

00:00:57.150 --> 00:00:58.300
"What?"

00:00:58.300 --> 00:01:00.609
"Game changer!

00:01:00.609 --> 00:01:03.070
Archie got hot!

00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:04.559
He's got abs now!"

00:01:04.559 --> 00:01:08.799
The comic version of Archie wasn't exactly
running around Riverdale showing off his six-pack,

00:01:08.799 --> 00:01:14.040
and, while he rocks some pretty great cheekbones
in the newer comics, classic Archie was much

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:15.380
more of a baby face.

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:18.850
Still, the show's fans don't seem to be complaining.

00:01:18.850 --> 00:01:19.850
Jughead Jones

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:24.619
Cole Sprouse made a huge transformation from
Suite Life child star to the angsty version

00:01:24.619 --> 00:01:27.100
of Jughead Jones shown on Riverdale.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:31.000
The actor had to dye his naturally blonde
hair dark brown for the part, although he

00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.020
keeps it slightly longer than Jughead does
in the comics.

00:01:34.020 --> 00:01:38.860
Still, Sprouse did a great job of adopting
Jughead's signature squint and beanie.

00:01:38.860 --> 00:01:42.970
The only real thing keeping him from being
a dead ringer from the character is the nose.

00:01:42.970 --> 00:01:47.910
In the original Archie comics, Jughead has
a Pinnochio-style nose, which Sprouse — thankfully

00:01:47.910 --> 00:01:49.250
— lacks.

00:01:49.250 --> 00:01:50.250
Fred Andrews

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:54.170
Archie's dad Fred in the comics is overweight
and nearly bald.

00:01:54.170 --> 00:01:59.299
But The CW decided to give Poppa Andrews a
little bit of an upgrade, casting former Beverly

00:01:59.299 --> 00:02:03.240
Hills, 90210 heartthrob Luke Perry in the
part.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:07.620
Perry's Fred is pretty buff, with a bit of
a beard and a messy hairstyle to match.

00:02:07.620 --> 00:02:11.860
He's also definitely not sporting the tiny
mustache Fred has in the comics.

00:02:11.860 --> 00:02:12.860
Which is fine.

00:02:12.860 --> 00:02:17.190
While we don't mind Perry's facial hair at
all, a bald Perry with a beer belly isn't

00:02:17.190 --> 00:02:18.440
really what anybody wants.

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:21.800
We feel old enough as it is just seeing him
be a dad.

00:02:21.800 --> 00:02:22.800
Cheryl Blossom

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:27.071
Cheryl Blossom gets a much bigger role in
Riverdale than in the Archie comics, where

00:02:27.071 --> 00:02:32.110
she mostly just serves as a supporting character
and further romantic rival for Archie.

00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:36.970
On the show, Cheryl and her brother Jason
are at the center of the show's murder mystery,

00:02:36.970 --> 00:02:40.550
and what Cheryl knows could end up being the
key to solving the crime.

00:02:40.550 --> 00:02:44.970
Like her comic book counterpart, Madelaine
Petsch is a redhead, although her hair is

00:02:44.970 --> 00:02:47.430
a bit darker than the character's bright locks.

00:02:47.430 --> 00:02:52.530
Petsch also has brown eyes, while Cheryl is
usually shown with green eyes in the comics.

00:02:52.530 --> 00:02:53.860
But we're not criticizing.

00:02:53.860 --> 00:02:57.790
After all, we've all seen what happens when
you end up on Cheryl's bad side.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:02:59.130
Kevin Keller

00:02:59.130 --> 00:03:04.730
Kevin is fairly new to the comics, introduced
in 2010 as the series' first openly gay character.

00:03:04.730 --> 00:03:09.520
In the comics, Kevin is blonde, as opposed
to actor Casey Cott, who has dark brown hair.

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.160
Cott also has green eyes, while in the comic,
they're blue.

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:16.390
So… he pretty much looks nothing like the
comics version of Kevin.

00:03:16.390 --> 00:03:17.390
But who cares?

00:03:17.390 --> 00:03:20.060
He just better keep making those snarky comments
directly to the audience.

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:24.210
"Should we maybe re-binge Making a Murderer
on Netflix tonight?"

00:03:24.210 --> 00:03:25.210
Betty Cooper

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:29.850
Riverdale's resident brilliant blonde is played
on the show by Lili Reinhart, who's shown

00:03:29.850 --> 00:03:32.960
she already has the character's sweet persona
down pat.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:37.550
However, while the actress does sport Betty's
signature blonde ponytail, her hair is a little

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:39.190
darker than the comics' yellow.

00:03:39.190 --> 00:03:42.630
She also doesn't have the bangs that Betty
is usually depicted with.

00:03:42.630 --> 00:03:47.970
Other than that, though, Reinhart is pretty
much a dead ringer for her classic character.

00:03:47.970 --> 00:03:48.970
Veronica Lodge

00:03:48.970 --> 00:03:53.580
Actress Camila Mendes said she wasn't planning
on auditioning for the part of Veronica until

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:58.700
she found out producers were making the character
Latina, a departure from her Caucasian background

00:03:58.700 --> 00:03:59.700
in the comics.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:04.730
Mendes, who is Brazilian, said she liked that
the character "wasn't a stereotype" of Latinas,

00:04:04.730 --> 00:04:06.590
which ended up attracting her to the role.

00:04:06.590 --> 00:04:11.200
Aside from Riverdale's change in Veronica's
background, Mendes is pretty much identical

00:04:11.200 --> 00:04:16.470
to her comic book counterpart, with the same
striking beauty and dark hair.

00:04:16.470 --> 00:04:17.470
Reggie Mantle

00:04:17.470 --> 00:04:22.610
Archie's comic book rival Reggie is played
by former Disney Channel actor Ross Butler

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:26.540
on Riverdale, changing the character's Caucasian
background to Eurasian.

00:04:26.540 --> 00:04:31.460
However, Butler definitely has the slicked-back
dark hair, cocky attitude, and good looks

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:34.650
to bring Riverdale's resident bad boy Reggie
to life.

00:04:34.650 --> 00:04:37.010
Now if only he'd get more screen time...

00:04:37.010 --> 00:04:38.340
Josie McCoy

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:43.720
Riverdale made the decision to make the entirety
of the Josie and the Pussycats lineup African-American

00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:46.720
— unlike the comics, which featured two
white characters.

00:04:46.720 --> 00:04:51.460
Ashleigh Murray leads the band as Josie McCoy,
embodying the character's signature sass,

00:04:51.460 --> 00:04:54.270
spunk, and musical talent pretty much perfectly.

00:04:54.270 --> 00:04:58.440
In the comics and cartoons, Josie is a yet
another redhead, only she also likes to wear

00:04:58.440 --> 00:05:02.260
cat ears and a cat suit while rocking out
— naturally.

00:05:02.260 --> 00:05:06.730
Riverdale moved away from the character's
outlandish style into more toned-down, fashion-forward

00:05:06.730 --> 00:05:11.530
outfits, which reflects the character's transition
from sweet girl to ambitious rocker.

00:05:11.530 --> 00:05:13.090
Which, y'know, rocks.

00:05:13.090 --> 00:05:14.650
Bah boom, sssss!

00:05:14.650 --> 00:05:15.930
Thanks for watching!

00:05:15.930 --> 00:05:18.870
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.370
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

